>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0;border-bottom:10px solid #f5f5f5\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>      <tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:20px 3.5% 10px;line-height:1.5\">\r\n<span class=\"b k\" style=\"font-size:27px;font-family:'gorditamedium',Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#222;letter-spacing:-0.1px;line-height:1.5\">  1 big thing: America&#x27;s love language </span>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>   <tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td> <img src=\"https://images.axios.com/LHLF93iUjjbt2MXqEr_XjlebB-s=/1920x1080/smart/2021/11/17/215917-1637186357217.jpg\" width=\"600\" style=\"width:100%\" id=\"item02\" alt=\"Illustration of a red hotline phone being buried under text messages. \"> </td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0\">\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:0 3.5%;line-height:1.3\">\r\n<span class=\"b\" style=\"font-size:13px;color:#848484\"> <p>Illustration: Aïda Amer/Axios</p> </span>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td height=\"15\" style=\"height:15px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr> <tr>\r\n<td class=\"v\" style=\"padding:0 3.5%;line-height:1.75;font-size:17px;font-family:Georgia,serif;color:#222;letter-spacing:-0.1px\"><p><strong>Texts can't replace</strong> in-person hangs or phone calls. But they've dramatically lowered the effort and coordination it takes to show people we care.</p><p>🧮 <strong>By the numbers: </strong>Texting is the most common way U.S. adults 54 and younger say they've shown someone they care in the past three months, <em>a new <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47549068.406679/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuaXBzb3MuY29tL2VuLXVzL2FtZXJpY2Fucy1zaG93LXdlLWNhcmUtdGV4dGluZz91dG1fc291cmNlPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXImdXRtX21lZGl1bT1lbWFpbCZ1dG1fY2FtcGFpZ249bmV3c2xldHRlcl9heGlvc2ZpbmlzaGxpbmUmc3RyZWFtPXRvcA/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aBe162a35b\" target=\"_blank\">Ipsos poll</a> found.</em></p><ul><li><strong>About two-thirds</strong> of adults in both the 18–34 and 35–54 age groups said they'd expressed care or appreciation via text.</li><li><strong>Texting is popular </strong>among older adults, too: 59% of those 55 and older said they'd used a text to show someone they care, compared with the 72% who'd done so with a phone call.</li></ul><p><strong>💡 Zoom in: </strong>The most meaningful text you send might be the random one.</p><ul><li><strong>Psychology research </strong><a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47549068.406679/aHR0cHM6Ly9wdWJtZWQubmNiaS5ubG0ubmloLmdvdi8zNTgxNjU2Ni8_dXRtX3NvdXJjZT1uZXdzbGV0dGVyJnV0bV9tZWRpdW09ZW1haWwmdXRtX2NhbXBhaWduPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXJfYXhpb3NmaW5pc2hsaW5lJnN0cmVhbT10b3A/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB7a0dfaab\" target=\"_blank\">shows</a> we routinely underestimate how much our friends — especially those we <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47549068.406679/aHR0cHM6Ly9wdWJtZWQubmNiaS5ubG0ubmloLmdvdi8zOTI0Mjc1OS8_dXRtX3NvdXJjZT1uZXdzbGV0dGVyJnV0bV9tZWRpdW09ZW1haWwmdXRtX2NhbXBhaWduPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXJfYXhpb3NmaW5pc2hsaW5lJnN0cmVhbT10b3A/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB46460029\" target=\"_blank\">haven't talked to in a while</a> — would love to hear from us \"just because.\"</li></ul><p><strong>🔎 The intrigue: </strong>Email and social media are going out of style as connection points, the poll found. </p><ul><li><strong>About 1 in 5 </strong>adults 54 and younger said they used emails to show care or appreciation.</li><li><strong>Roughly the same share </strong>shouted out their friends and family on social media.</li></ul><p><em><a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47549068.406679/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuaXBzb3MuY29tL2VuLXVzL2FtZXJpY2Fucy1zaG93LXdlLWNhcmUtdGV4dGluZz91dG1fc291cmNlPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXImdXRtX21lZGl1bT1lbWFpbCZ1dG1fY2FtcGFpZ249bmV3c2xldHRlcl9heGlvc2ZpbmlzaGxpbmUmc3RyZWFtPXRvcA/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aCe162a35b\" target=\"_blank\">Explore the data</a>.</em></p></td>\r\n</tr> <tr><td align=\"center\" style=\"padding:20px 3.5% 25